# Generated by scripts/celegans_fates.py (genomeos.organism.fate_rules): terminal fates from the
# measured factors (Ma et al. 2021), read as integrated along the lineage path. Imported after the lineage program, so a
# factor rule overrides the observed fate of a terminal cell and the lookup stays the fallback.
# Precedence is the `priority` of each decision (first rule highest; the lookup has 0) under
# `regime { fates: first }`, declared by the importing program.
module organism.celegans.fates
import cell_types.bio

decision factor_fate_00 { action: differentiate; when: cell_type = Coelomocyte|Epithelium|Excretory|Gland|GliaSheath|GliaSocket|Hypodermis|Intestine|Mesoderm|Muscle|Neuron|Other|PharyngealMarginal|Rectal|Reproductive|TailSpike|Valve, stage = Cleavage|Gastrulation|Morphogenesis, ELT-2_integrated = present; to: Intestine; priority: 25; evidence: experimental "Fukushige et al. 1998, Dev Biol 198:286; Sommermann et al. 2010, Dev Biol 347:154; factors Ma et al. 2021, Nat Methods 18:893 (Zenodo 4737593)"; confidence: 0.8 }
